Research Process for Q1: Which docx-js Properties Survive GDocs Import Intact
Phase 1 — Source Triage (Desk Research)

Priority order:

Google's OOXML import spec documentation — Google has published (partially) what it supports from the OOXML standard. Start here to bound the search space.
OOXML spec itself (ECMA-376) — Identifies which properties are standard vs. extension; GDocs is more likely to drop non-standard extensions silently.
docx-js source / issue tracker — Search open and closed issues tagged with "Google Docs," "import," or "corruption." Contributors often document breakage empirically.
Stack Overflow / GitHub Discussions — Secondary empirical reports; lower reliability but high coverage of edge cases.

Expected yield: Partial. Likely covers common properties (fonts, basic paragraph styles) but will have gaps on table shading, background, and run-level color specifically.

Phase 2 — Empirical Matrix Test (Primary Method)

Since authoritative documentation is incomplete, the real answer requires a controlled generation-and-import experiment.

Design:

Generate one minimal .docx per property under test — isolate variables
Import each into Google Docs
Inspect the result visually and via GDocs → Download as .docx → parse the round-tripped XML to see what GDocs preserved, modified, or dropped
Log outcome per property: passes clean / corrupted / silently dropped / falls back to default

Property categories to test:

Category	Specific Properties
Table cell shading	ShadingType.CLEAR, SOLID, NIL + fill hex
Document background	Document.background color
Run-level color	TextRun.color
Paragraph style color	paragraphStyles color
Borders	Cell borders, page borders
Font properties	Family, size, bold, italic
Phase 3 — XML Diff Analysis
Use a tool (Python python-docx or raw unzip + grep) to diff the input .docx XML against the round-tripped GDocs export
Identifies exactly which XML nodes GDocs preserves vs. rewrites vs. drops
This is the highest-signal method — behavioral ground truth
Phase 4 — Synthesis
Produce a confirmed safe/broken/unknown matrix
Answers Q1 directly and also unblocks Q2–9

Bottleneck: Phase 2 requires generating and manually importing ~15–20 test documents. Time-intensive but non-substitutable given documentation gaps.

